[Chapter "Against ...c6"]
[Line "Same plan against ...c6 and ...Bf5"]
[Opening "Rapport-Jobava System"]

{When Black plays ...c6, Nb5 doesn't work, so White uses the pawn plan instead.} 1. d4 {Start with the queen's pawn.} 1... d5 2. Nc3 {The Jobava idea: the knight comes to c3 before the c-pawn moves, ready for Nb5 or e4.} 2... Nf6 3. Bf4 {Develop the bishop outside the pawn chain before e3.} 3... c6 {Black takes b5 away from the knight.} 4. e3 {Solid development.} 4... Bf5 5. f3 {Preparing g4.} 5... e6 6. g4 {Chase the bishop.} 6... Bg6 7. h4 {Keep pushing: h5 is next, and the bishop is running out of squares.} *
